## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | Add assertions | Eliminates false-pass risk |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | Split into deterministic tests | Closes hidden test gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `await` the async call | Eliminates flakiness + speeds CI |
| 4 | Mystery Guest | Inline test data | Fixes portability / CI failures |
| 5 | Exception Handling | Use `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` | Quick 1-min refactor |
| 6 | Eager Test | Isolate or mark as integration | Improves failure diagnosis |
| 7 | Magic Number + Assertion Roulette | Named constants + messages | Improves readability |
| 8 | Sensitive Equality | Assert on structured properties | Reduces fragility |
| 9 | General Fixture | Remove unused `_logger` | Minor cleanup |
| 10 | Lazy Test | Evaluate parameterization | Low priority |

**Bottom line:** 8 of 9 tests carry at least one academic smell; 4 are high-severity (false-pass risk, flakiness, hidden gaps). Priorities 1–4 are the critical fixes — they address tests that can silently pass when the production code is broken.
